course: dictionary
lesson: 13455
title: The word hue
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A hue is a colour, or a shade of a colour. Red, blue and green are colours. A reddish hue is a red that is a little different, like the colour of a rose or a brick.
explain: «The sky turned a rosy hue as the sun went down.» The clues are sky, sun going down and rosy, which is a soft pink-red. So hue must mean colour here. Check by swapping: «The sky turned a rosy colour as the sun went down» still makes sense.
explain: Hue has two other meanings, but you will meet them less often. In a formal sentence, a hue is a kind or type, as in «people of every political hue». The old phrase hue and cry means a loud, noisy protest.
fact: A hue is a colour or a shade of a colour.
fact: «Hue» is a noun. You can say a hue or two hues.
fact: Artists mix paints to make new hues.
fact: The colours of the rainbow are hues.
fact: «Hue and cry» is an old phrase for a loud, noisy protest.
exercise: «The sky turned a rosy hue as the sun went down.» What is a hue? | A kind of cloud | A small bird | *A colour or shade of a colour | A loud noise
exercise: «Mia mixed blue and yellow to find a new green hue.» What did Mia make? | A loud protest | A tall tree | A rainy day | *A new shade of green
exercise: Ben says hue always means a loud noise. What is the right meaning of hue in most sentences? | A piece of music | A large room | *A colour or shade of a colour | A loud, noisy protest
test: «Every hue of the rainbow was painted on the wall.» What does every hue mean here? | Every window | *Every colour | Every sound | Every bird
test: «People of every political hue came to the meeting.» What does hue mean in this sentence? | *A kind or type | A big room | A loud protest | A colour
exam: Which of these is a hue? | *A deep blue like the sea | A small drum | A cup of warm milk | A long walk to school
